.TH EVOXD 1 "2026-10-10" "evoxd 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
evoxd, evoxd-gui \- disposable KVM VMs for e-mail and web browsing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B evoxd
.RI { setup | template-import | template-list | template-verify | template-remove | start | list | stop | console | reconcile | netcheck } " ..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts one-time virtual machines named DISPOSABLE-<PURPOSE>-NN from a protected copy of a
TEMPLATE-<SYSTEM> domain. Stopping a VM destroys it. Data lives in /srv/evoxd.
See
.B evoxd --help
for details.
.SH MEMORY
Before every start (GUI and
.BR "evoxd start" )
the free memory is checked with MemAvailable. Each VM needs its RAM plus 256 MiB overhead.
If less than the host reserve would stay available, a warning is shown; if less than half
the reserve would stay available, the start is refused.
.SH TEMPLATES
.B evoxd template-remove NAME
.RB [ --version
.IR N " | " --older ]
deletes imported copies in the pool evoxd-templates and their registry entries. The original
TEMPLATE-* domain and VAULT-* are never touched. Refused while any VM (registry or libvirt)
uses the copy as backing file.
.PP
.B evoxd template-verify
compares the SHA-256 of a copy with the value from the import. A mismatch marks the copy
DAMAGED; no new VMs start from it until it is imported again or removed. The check detects
changes of the file after the import (disk errors, tampering on the host). It does not detect
malware that was already in the template before the import.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/evoxd/config.json
Optional settings, e.g.
.B {"host_reserve_mib": 2048}
(host reserve in MiB, 512\(en65536, default 2048) and
.B {"verify_after_shutdown": true}
(GUI: verify the template in the background after each disposable VM ends; default false).
